{"effects":[{"path":["profile_default"],"knob":"profile_default","before":"spine","after":"deep","direction":"raise","sentence":"profile_default: spine → deep. Starting every issue on deep adds the target-graph and SDK checks, about two more short passes per issue."},{"path":["gates","plan-review"],"knob":"gates.plan-review","before":"lite","after":"on","direction":"raise","sentence":"gates.plan-review: lite → on. Plans now get the full review before any code, adding about one review round."},{"path":["gates","research"],"knob":"gates.research","before":"off","after":"lite","direction":"raise","sentence":"gates.research: off → lite. Each such library gets a pinned docs cache and one executed call, a short research pass."},{"path":["signoff","one-way"],"knob":"signoff.one-way","before":null,"after":"human","direction":"change","sentence":"signoff.one-way: unset → human. Who approves a one-way door: a change that is hard to undo. human: A human approves it before it closes."},{"path":["signoff","unlock"],"knob":"signoff.unlock","before":"off","after":"on","direction":"lower","sentence":"signoff.unlock: off → on. Switching unlock on lets registered surfaces unlock one-way actions once their bar gates, audit baseline and budget hold."},{"path":["signoff","raise","*","merge"],"knob":"signoff.raise.*.merge","before":null,"after":["adversarial-review:max"],"direction":"raise","sentence":"signoff.raise.*.merge: unset → adversarial-review:max. The agent must pass more gates before it may merge a one-way change alone. Adds adversarial-review:max."},{"path":["close","tpm-report"],"knob":"close.tpm-report","before":"file-only","after":"on","direction":"raise","sentence":"close.tpm-report: file-only → on. Each close ends with a refreshed project report."},{"path":["ceilings","all"],"knob":"ceilings.all","before":null,"after":"R1","direction":"raise","sentence":"ceilings.all: unset → R1. A lower ceiling (toward R0) makes more changes wait for a human sign-off before they close."},{"path":["lifts","U0"],"knob":"lifts.U0","before":null,"after":"R2","direction":"lower","sentence":"lifts.U0: unset → R2. Low-risk bleed fixes close with review after the fact (R1) or automatically (R2); never U2 or U3."},{"path":["remediate","on"],"knob":"remediate.on","before":["final-gates-fail"],"after":["final-gates-fail","unlock-gate-fail"],"direction":"lower","sentence":"remediate.on: final-gates-fail → final-gates-fail, unlock-gate-fail. More triggers: more failures are first handed to an agent loop to fix. Adds unlock-gate-fail: A gate a surface's one-way unlock requires failed."},{"path":["remediate","max_rounds"],"knob":"remediate.max_rounds","before":2,"after":4,"direction":"lower","sentence":"remediate.max_rounds: 2 → 4. More rounds: the loop keeps trying longer, using agent time, before a human looks."},{"path":["ask","two_way_timeout"],"knob":"ask.two_way_timeout","before":"24h","after":"none","direction":"change","sentence":"ask.two_way_timeout: 24h → none. How long a two-way ask with a recommendation waits before it is answered with that recommendation: none (default), or <n>h from 4 to 720. A one-way ask never times out."},{"path":["ask","digest"],"knob":"ask.digest","before":"off","after":"hourly","direction":"change","sentence":"ask.digest: off → hourly. How non-blocking asks are rolled up for the operator: off (default), hourly, daily. hourly: Non-blocking asks are rolled into one hourly digest."},{"path":["ask","session_budget"],"knob":"ask.session_budget","before":5,"after":2,"direction":"raise","sentence":"ask.session_budget: 5 → 2. A smaller budget: a session must wait for answers before it asks more."},{"path":["user_impact","U1"],"knob":"user_impact.U1","before":["revert-path"],"after":["revert-path","e2e"],"direction":"raise","sentence":"user_impact.U1: revert-path → revert-path, e2e. Each U1 change owes more evidence before it closes, each item a real run or rehearsal. Adds e2e: An end-to-end run against the real stack."}]}
